if you set out the vision
and you execute the vision

00:11:12.905 --> 00:11:15.641 align:start size:88% position:13%
and you do well, people
will follow that.

00:11:15.641 --> 00:11:16.942
And that's what they wanna see.

00:11:16.942 --> 00:11:20.379 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so that was
just my philosophy.

00:11:20.379 --> 00:11:23.215 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so when it came
for like Covid,

00:11:23.215 --> 00:11:25.951
you know I remember like you
know just getting hammered

00:11:25.951 --> 00:11:28.454
by corporate press and
they politicized it.

00:11:28.454 --> 00:11:30.423
They wanted to use
it to take out Trump.

00:11:30.423 --> 00:11:32.625
They wanted to use it to
take out people like me.

00:11:32.625 --> 00:11:34.660
And that's just what they do.

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:36.796
But you know my view was okay,

00:11:36.796 --> 00:11:41.801
if by me protecting the jobs
of all the people I represent,

00:11:43.302 --> 00:11:45.938
ends up putting my own job
in jeopardy then so be it.

00:11:45.938 --> 00:11:48.541 align:start size:81% position:19%
Let the chips fall
where they may.

00:11:48.541 --> 00:11:51.510
I wasn't worried about politics

00:11:51.510 --> 00:11:56.482 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I would totally be willing
to because look I have,

00:11:57.950 --> 00:11:58.918 align:start size:97% position:3%
there's great, there's a lot
of opportunities in life.

00:11:58.918 --> 00:12:01.053
It isn't like I have to do this.

00:12:01.053 --> 00:12:03.289
And so if it didn't
work out for me,

00:12:03.289 --> 00:12:05.691
I would've been totally
great being able to look

00:12:05.691 --> 00:12:07.326
in the mirror and
say you know what,

00:12:07.326 --> 00:12:09.095
I did what I thought was right

00:12:09.095 --> 00:12:10.796 align:start size:84% position:16%
to benefit the
people I represent.

00:12:10.796 --> 00:12:12.998 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think when you get in
situations where some of these

00:12:12.998 --> 00:12:15.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
politicians, you know they
get paralyzed by polls

00:12:15.067 --> 00:12:17.770
and consultants and everything,

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:20.573
and then they don't
do what they think

00:12:20.573 --> 00:12:23.109 align:start position:0%
in their guts right because
they're worried about blow back.

00:12:23.109 --> 00:12:24.410
They're worried about the media.

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:26.812
They're worried about
political consequences.

00:12:26.812 --> 00:12:28.347
Well then guess what happens?

00:12:28.347 --> 00:12:30.616
You end up not succeeding
most of the time anyways,

00:12:30.616 --> 00:12:32.218
then you end up looking
in the mirror like man,

00:12:32.218 --> 00:12:34.820 align:start size:97% position:3%
I just wish I would've
followed what I believed in.

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:37.556
And so you know, no regrets,

00:12:37.556 --> 00:12:38.591
you gotta do what
you think is right.

00:12:38.591 --> 00:12:41.494
And in this case with Florida I,

00:12:42.895 --> 00:12:47.466 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know with Covid I actually
consumed the data myself.

00:12:48.601 --> 00:12:50.069 align:start size:84% position:16%
I didn't just, I
wasn't just, you know,

00:12:50.069 --> 00:12:53.072 align:start position:0%
saying if Fauci says something,
then you got a genuflect.

00:12:53.072 --> 00:12:54.807 align:start size:84% position:16%
What are they
getting at the data?

00:12:56.342 --> 00:12:59.311 align:start position:0%
And the fact is Fauci was wrong
about a lot of this stuff.

00:12:59.311 --> 00:13:01.614 align:start size:69% position:31%
Okay.
(cheering)

00:13:04.116 --> 00:13:07.153
We were the first big state
to guarantee every parent

00:13:07.153 --> 00:13:09.355
the ability to send their
kid to school in person,

00:13:09.355 --> 00:13:12.691
way back in 2020, right?

00:13:12.691 --> 00:13:16.428 align:start size:84% position:16%
Fauci opposed us
having kids in school.

00:13:16.428 --> 00:13:19.799
He opposed what we were doing
when we had businesses open

00:13:19.799 --> 00:13:23.035
and protecting people's jobs
and were having these events.

00:13:23.035 --> 00:13:25.504
He opposed us every
step of the way.

00:13:25.504 --> 00:13:28.874
And so that wasn't based on
data because the schooling

00:13:28.874 --> 00:13:31.544
was obvious that you needed
to have the kids in school.

00:13:31.544 --> 00:13:33.946
It was based more on ideology

00:13:33.946 --> 00:13:36.615
and it was more based on
all these other things.

00:13:36.615 --> 00:13:39.852 align:start size:88% position:13%
So we were right to have
to stand up to Fauci.

00:13:41.287 --> 00:13:43.923
- We'll respect your free
speech if you respect ours,

00:13:43.923 --> 00:13:46.125
but you gotta do it outside.

00:13:46.125 --> 00:13:48.027
You gotta do it outside.

00:13:48.027 --> 00:13:50.629
- So at the end of the day
that's just my philosophy.

00:13:50.629 --> 00:13:52.131
And I would just,

00:13:52.131 --> 00:13:55.067
I think that you gotta do
what you think is right.

00:13:55.067 --> 00:13:58.470
I tend to, you know if
there's a choice between

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:01.273
going against the machine
and siding with the folks

00:14:01.273 --> 00:14:02.741
I'm gonna side with the folks.

00:14:02.741 --> 00:14:04.577
And here's the thing, I think,

00:14:04.577 --> 00:14:08.981
that I think people get it
more than they ever have.

00:14:08.981 --> 00:14:12.585 align:start position:0%
They understand you look at
some of these elite bureaucrats

00:14:12.585 --> 00:14:15.421
like Fauci, you look at the
corporate media, big tech,

00:14:15.421 --> 00:14:17.890
the emperor has no clothes.

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:20.025
These are discredited
elites in our country

00:14:20.025 --> 00:14:23.462
and they don't have your
best interest at heart.

00:14:23.462 --> 00:14:26.432 align:start size:97% position:3%
They don't have this state's
best interest at heart.

00:14:26.432 --> 00:14:28.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sometimes though it
doesn't feel like you know

00:14:28.834 --> 00:14:32.338 align:start position:0%
your voice can be heard because
so much of it is dominated

00:14:32.338 --> 00:14:33.939
by this one viewpoint.

00:14:33.939 --> 00:14:36.575
But when you stand up and
you stand in that fire

00:14:36.575 --> 00:14:39.044
and you fight back
for people, man,

00:14:39.044 --> 00:14:40.613
they will have your back.

00:14:40.613 --> 00:14:41.914
They will support you

00:14:43.449 --> 00:14:45.451
and that's what we've shown
in the state of Florida.

00:14:45.451 --> 00:14:47.686
(cheering)

00:15:03.869 --> 00:15:06.338 align:start size:69% position:31%
See.
(applause)

00:15:13.579 --> 00:15:16.982
- He doesn't like polls, but
standing ovations ain't bad.

00:15:16.982 --> 00:15:19.218
You know, those are pretty good.

00:15:19.218 --> 00:15:20.085
I got an idea.

00:15:21.253 --> 00:15:22.488
So, you know if you
weren't a politician,

00:15:22.488 --> 00:15:23.756
well, how about this maybe?

00:15:23.756 --> 00:15:24.990
And you guys could
chime in on this.

00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:26.759 align:start size:88% position:13%
We don't have to put the
governor on the spot,

00:15:26.759 --> 00:15:29.094
but maybe like, you know you
crush it in this next election

00:15:29.094 --> 00:15:29.929
here in Florida.

00:15:31.297 --> 00:15:33.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's do maybe eight
years in the White House.

00:15:33.132 --> 00:15:34.466 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then you become
CEO of Disney.

00:15:34.466 --> 00:15:35.968
How does that sound?

00:15:35.968 --> 00:15:38.237
(cheering)

00:15:42.708 --> 00:15:43.742 align:start size:84% position:16%
- You know who
knows what happens?

00:15:43.742 --> 00:15:46.478
You never know in life so.

00:15:46.478 --> 00:15:48.914
- Alright so, so let's talk
about some of the other stuff

00:15:48.914 --> 00:15:50.382
that you're doing,

00:15:50.382 --> 00:15:52.017 align:start position:0%
'cause you really are doing
stuff here that is not happening

00:15:52.017 --> 00:15:53.385
in the rest of the country.

00:15:53.385 --> 00:15:55.721 align:start position:0%
You just signed this fatherhood
bill last month here.

00:15:55.721 --> 00:15:58.557
This is just another
issue that you took on

00:15:58.557 --> 00:16:00.993
that seemingly we
need to talk about,

00:16:00.993 --> 00:16:04.096
we don't talk about honestly
and you chose to fight it.

00:16:04.096 --> 00:16:06.365 align:start size:84% position:16%
So tell me a little
bit about that.

00:16:06.365 --> 00:16:09.335
- Yeah I mean I think that if
you look at what's going on

00:16:09.335 --> 00:16:11.203
in our, in our society.

00:16:13.038 --> 00:16:15.674
(yelling)

00:16:15.674 --> 00:16:17.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did they have to at
least pay to get in here?

00:16:17.576 --> 00:16:19.912
- Oh they had to pay.
- Good, good, good.

00:16:19.912 --> 00:16:22.181
(cheering)

00:16:23.615 --> 00:16:26.685
I mean like, look, I get
people have their shtick.

00:16:26.685 --> 00:16:29.021 align:start size:97% position:3%
I get people, you know do
things a little bit different

00:16:29.021 --> 00:16:31.256
on that side than we would.

00:16:31.256 --> 00:16:33.692
But honestly it's
so ineffective.

00:16:33.692 --> 00:16:36.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nobody, all you do is
tick people off when you,

00:16:36.328 --> 00:16:37.997 align:start size:84% position:16%
you try to interrupt
these events.

00:16:37.997 --> 00:16:41.000
So keep doing it, you're just
gonna help us in the long run.

00:16:43.102 --> 00:16:44.703
But.

00:16:44.703 --> 00:16:49.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
- And you live in
Florida, Florida, people.

00:16:49.308 --> 00:16:52.011 align:start size:81% position:19%
- But you know
the fatherhood is,

00:16:52.011 --> 00:16:53.879 align:start size:84% position:16%
is interesting
because if you look at

00:16:53.879 --> 00:16:56.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
all the different problems
society could deal with

00:16:56.849 --> 00:17:00.119
a huge number of them are
rooted in kids growing up

00:17:00.119 --> 00:17:02.788
without having a
father in the home

00:17:02.788 --> 00:17:07.793 align:start size:97% position:3%
and so I started getting
involved in this when I was,

00:17:07.793 --> 00:17:10.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
my first year as governor,
we're doing the budget.

00:17:10.162 --> 00:17:12.631
There was some money for a
group called All Pro Dads

00:17:12.631 --> 00:17:14.900 align:start size:81% position:19%
and it was founded
by former Bucks

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:17.636
and Colt's head coach Tony
Dungy who's a great guy.

00:17:18.837 --> 00:17:21.073
And Tony and you know look,

00:17:21.073 --> 00:17:23.375 align:start size:81% position:19%
I just signed next
year's budget.

00:17:24.743 --> 00:17:28.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
I vetoed a world, Florida
record $3.1 billion.

00:17:28.814 --> 00:17:31.917
Before I became governor the
record was like $800 million.

00:17:31.917 --> 00:17:35.154 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so we're, we're very
tough and I mean we will veto

00:17:35.154 --> 00:17:37.222
and so you can veto
individual items.

00:17:37.222 --> 00:17:39.324 line:0%
And so he called me just to
kind of like make the pitch

00:17:39.324 --> 00:17:42.928 line:0%
and you know I'm like
honestly, I trust you.

00:17:42.928 --> 00:17:44.763 line:0%
I know you're gonna, your
heart's in the right place.

00:17:44.763 --> 00:17:45.697
And I know this is important.

00:17:45.697 --> 00:17:47.633
So we started getting involved.

00:17:47.633 --> 00:17:49.101
We'd work with private groups,

00:17:49.101 --> 00:17:50.903
we'd work with our state
agencies and then this year

00:17:50.903 --> 00:17:54.073 align:start size:84% position:16%
kind of a more
comprehensive thing.

00:17:54.073 --> 00:17:55.007
But if you talk to coach Dungy

00:17:55.007 --> 00:17:56.442
and he was at the bill signing.

00:17:57.776 --> 00:17:59.311 align:start size:97% position:3%
When he said when he
became Tampa Bay head coach

00:17:59.311 --> 00:18:01.747
he went to minister at some
of the prisons and he looked

00:18:01.747 --> 00:18:02.781
and he said you know,

00:18:04.216 --> 00:18:06.585
I noticed that it wasn't
because of poverty, race,

00:18:06.585 --> 00:18:07.853
all these other things.

00:18:09.288 --> 00:18:11.223
The reason these people were
in prison was because they did

00:18:11.223 --> 00:18:13.625
not have a father
figure in the home.

00:18:13.625 --> 00:18:15.627
And if you could address that,

00:18:15.627 --> 00:18:19.164 align:start size:97% position:3%
you would have so much better
luck in society overall.

00:18:19.164 --> 00:18:21.066
And so that's what
we're trying to do.

00:18:22.201 --> 00:18:23.635 align:start size:84% position:16%
And part of it is
resources, education.

00:18:23.635 --> 00:18:26.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
Part of it though is
sending a message to men,

00:18:26.405 --> 00:18:28.774
meet your responsibilities.

00:18:28.774 --> 00:18:30.776
You have a responsibility.

00:18:32.044 --> 00:18:34.346
And I can tell you,

00:18:36.081 --> 00:18:38.383 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know one of the
reasons I ran for governor,

00:18:38.383 --> 00:18:41.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was a member of
Congress for a few terms.

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:43.255
And I first got elected.

00:18:43.255 --> 00:18:45.257
It was just my wife and me.

00:18:45.257 --> 00:18:46.658
Second election it was
just my wife and me.

00:18:46.658 --> 00:18:49.862
Well then after the
third election, 2016,

00:18:49.862 --> 00:18:52.831
we had our first child,
our daughter Madison.

00:18:52.831 --> 00:18:55.534
And so I'm in DC
thinking to myself,

00:18:55.534 --> 00:18:56.668
you travel back and forth.

00:18:56.668 --> 00:18:58.837
I'm like, why am I up here?

00:18:58.837 --> 00:19:00.405
You know, I really
want to be back home.

00:19:00.405 --> 00:19:02.808 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so as with
governor, you know,

00:19:02.808 --> 00:19:04.610
we see him every day.

00:19:04.610 --> 00:19:07.179 align:start size:88% position:13%
We're able to be present
and I'm very busy.

00:19:07.179 --> 00:19:10.115
I'm much busier in this job
than a Congressman would be.

00:19:10.115 --> 00:19:12.484
But because we're all
in the same state,

00:19:12.484 --> 00:19:15.087 align:start size:97% position:3%
all in the, you know obviously
living in Tallahassee now,

00:19:15.087 --> 00:19:16.922
you're able to do it.

00:19:16.922 --> 00:19:18.724
So my wife and I put a
lot of emphasis on that

00:19:18.724 --> 00:19:19.725
but particularly me.

00:19:20.759 --> 00:19:22.761
They're, they're just, you know,

00:19:22.761 --> 00:19:24.129 align:start size:97% position:3%
my wife does some great things
that I don't do as good in,

00:19:25.464 --> 00:19:27.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I offer just something
else in terms of,

00:19:27.432 --> 00:19:30.335
in terms of for the
kids to look up to.

00:19:30.335 --> 00:19:32.271
So I think it's essential.

00:19:32.271 --> 00:19:33.672 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I've said if we
could snap our fingers,

00:19:33.672 --> 00:19:35.807
every kid grows up
in America with a,

00:19:35.807 --> 00:19:37.643
with a good father in the home,

00:19:37.643 --> 00:19:40.612
we would not be talking about
a lot of these other problems,

00:19:40.612 --> 00:19:43.115 align:start size:69% position:31%
no way.
(applause)

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:51.223
- So as a new Floridian one of
the things that's constantly

00:19:51.223 --> 00:19:53.592
on my mind is what can
I do for this state?

00:19:53.592 --> 00:19:56.795
And I really mean that, what
can I do for this state that I,

00:19:56.795 --> 00:19:57.996
I feel like a refugee.

00:19:57.996 --> 00:19:59.164
I am a refugee.

00:20:00.599 --> 00:20:03.802
It, I genuinely feel like
I came from another country

00:20:03.802 --> 00:20:05.771 align:start size:84% position:16%
and thank God you guys
speak English here.

00:20:05.771 --> 00:20:09.208
That's basically, that's
basically where I'm at.

00:20:09.208 --> 00:20:11.543
But so what do we do, what
do we do to defend Florida?

00:20:11.543 --> 00:20:14.046
Because the more that
Florida does it right.

00:20:14.046 --> 00:20:16.515
The more that the machine,

00:20:16.515 --> 00:20:19.318
whether that's the media
or the political machine,

00:20:19.318 --> 00:20:21.053
or just the elite machine,
whatever you wanna call it,

00:20:21.053 --> 00:20:21.887
the more it is going
to stare down you,

00:20:21.887 --> 00:20:23.155
stare down these folks.

00:20:23.155 --> 00:20:25.757
What do we do to just
keep this state right?

00:20:26.925 --> 00:20:28.093 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, I think it's
a great question.

00:20:28.093 --> 00:20:29.328
And before I answer it

00:20:29.328 --> 00:20:30.529 align:start size:84% position:16%
just let me say this
about California.

00:20:30.529 --> 00:20:33.098
So first time.

00:20:33.098 --> 00:20:36.168 align:start size:97% position:3%
- You gotta put money in the
jar man, that's the deal.

00:20:36.168 --> 00:20:37.736
- So Covid hits.

00:20:38.937 --> 00:20:41.273
First time I went to
California since Covid

00:20:41.273 --> 00:20:43.875
was June of 2021.

00:20:43.875 --> 00:20:46.178
So over a year into
Covid but you know

00:20:46.178 --> 00:20:47.346
they still had mandates.

00:20:48.547 --> 00:20:50.048
They had, it was
not like Florida.

00:20:50.048 --> 00:20:51.416 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I, so I'm out there doing
stuff like fundraising,

00:20:51.416 --> 00:20:52.951
all this stuff.

00:20:52.951 --> 00:20:54.620
And I told myself, I'm like
look, I'm not wearing a mask.

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:55.854
I'm gonna do my thing.

00:20:55.854 --> 00:20:57.556 align:start size:84% position:16%
So you put me wherever
you wanna put me,

00:20:57.556 --> 00:20:58.857
but just understand.

00:21:00.259 --> 00:21:01.860 align:start size:97% position:3%
I don't want any confrontation
or anything but this is,

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:02.694
I'm gonna live like
I live in Florida.

00:21:02.694 --> 00:21:03.862
So I get there.

00:21:03.862 --> 00:21:05.030 align:start size:84% position:16%
First day I'm
there, I'm waiting.

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:06.331 align:start size:84% position:16%
The cars are coming
to pick me up.

00:21:06.331 --> 00:21:07.833
I'm on the curb.

00:21:07.833 --> 00:21:10.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
These two guys in masks
come scurrying over to me.

00:21:10.369 --> 00:21:11.770
I'm like oh God, here we go.

00:21:13.472 --> 00:21:16.675
One guy gets right in front
of me, pulls down his mask,

00:21:16.675 --> 00:21:18.810
looks me right in
the eye and says,

00:21:18.810 --> 00:21:20.212
I wish you were our governor.

00:21:20.212 --> 00:21:21.847
Put on the mask and left.

00:21:21.847 --> 00:21:24.850
So you never know.

00:21:24.850 --> 00:21:27.085
(cheering)

00:21:30.322 --> 00:21:32.057
And so it was interesting.

00:21:33.725 --> 00:21:37.329
But what I would say is
when you're looking at.

00:21:39.898 --> 00:21:43.368 align:start size:84% position:16%
Big time fail buddy,
big time fail.

00:21:43.368 --> 00:21:45.504
(jeering)

00:21:49.775 --> 00:21:53.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know part of what
we're doing I think now is

00:21:53.512 --> 00:21:56.548 align:start size:88% position:13%
